[h1]TECZ | SPARDA MODS[/h1]
[b]ROLEPLAY • PVE • HARDCORE[/b]

A curated server-specific package for TECZ, a DayZ roleplay and hardcore PvE project. This Workshop item bundles licensed third-party modules for use in the TECZ environment, with all original creators credited below.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TecPlayBR/DayZ/main/TECZ/SteamWorkshop/assets/01-about.jpg[/img]
[h2]ABOUT THE PACKAGE[/h2]
[b]Package contents:[/b] 16 packaged PBO files, including associated data, texture and shortcut components.
[b]Original creator:[/b] Sparda / Sparda Mods.
[b]Status:[/b] TECZ Season 1 in development.

[b]Please note:[/b] A module being included in this package does not guarantee that its mechanics, items, services or events are enabled on the server.

[h2]PACKAGE CONTENTS[/h2]
[h3]COMMUNITY & ROLEPLAY[/h3]
[list]
[*] Billboards: in-world visual boards
[*] Prison: prison cells and detention management
[*] VIP Panel: role-based kits and customization
[*] Item Private: private item access rules
[/list]

[h3]TRADE & CUSTOMIZATION[/h3]
[list]
[*] Store: in-game shop systems
[*] Skin Store: appearance shop
[*] Skin Textures: associated appearance resources
[/list]

[h3]INTERFACE & EXPERIENCE[/h3]
[list]
[*] Kill Feed: event messaging and optional indicators
[*] Safe Inventory: protected inventory access
[*] Color Alive: visual module included in the package; exact behavior may vary by configuration
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TecPlayBR/DayZ/main/TECZ/SteamWorkshop/assets/02-screenshots.jpg[/img]
[h2]GAMEPLAY GALLERY[/h2]
Screenshots of the actual TECZ gameplay and individual systems will be shown in this Workshop item's image gallery as they are tested. Artwork and development previews do not represent a guarantee that a feature is active.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TecPlayBR/DayZ/main/TECZ/SteamWorkshop/assets/03-installation.jpg[/img]
[h2]INSTALLATION & REQUIREMENTS[/h2]
[list]
[*] Subscribe to the TECZ Workshop items required by the server.
[*] Use the official DayZ Launcher to join TECZ and manage the required Workshop dependencies.
[*] Do not assume that a module's presence means all its optional integrations are configured or enabled.
[*] For installation support, contact the official TECZ community.
[/list]

